Subject: Adapt kubescape v3 to the moby/buildkit DockerAuthProviderConfig API
Origin: DHI-internal (buildkit API compatibility for the v3 line)
Description: BuildKit v0.28.1 replaced DockerAuthProviderConfig.ConfigFile with AuthConfigProvider. Use authprovider.LoadAuthConfig so the kubescape v3 patch command compiles against the BuildKit version the v3 go.mod resolves to.
Base-Tree: git https://github.com/kubescape/kubescape.git 6ce0121a03697a6976656fe1f13dbb171a1610a9
Verify: cmd `go build ./core/core/ && echo ok` expect "ok"
Forwarded: not-needed (v3 source predates the BuildKit API change; DHI build compatibility only)
Drop-When: never: the v3 line pins kubescape 3.0.48, which still uses the removed ConfigFile field

The go/bump step raises moby/buildkit to v0.31.1 for this line. Upstream kubescape v3 still constructs DockerAuthProviderConfig with ConfigFile, which no longer compiles against that BuildKit release. The hunk keeps the same credential source (the default docker config file) and only changes how it is handed to BuildKit.

--- a/core/core/patch.go
+++ b/core/core/patch.go
@@ -198,7 +198,7 @@
 	defer bkClient.Close()
 
 	dockerConfig := config.LoadDefaultConfigFile(os.Stderr)
-	cfg := authprovider.DockerAuthProviderConfig{ConfigFile: dockerConfig}
+	cfg := authprovider.DockerAuthProviderConfig{AuthConfigProvider: authprovider.LoadAuthConfig(dockerConfig)}
 	attachable := []session.Attachable{authprovider.NewDockerAuthProvider(cfg)}
 	solveOpt := client.SolveOpt{
 		Exports: []client.ExportEntry{
